 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508073,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Solve <span data-math=\"-13m \\geq 65\">-13m \\geq 65</span>, graph the solution on the number line, and write the solution in interval notation.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>First solve the inequality.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\" - 13m \\ge 65\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide by –13.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{ - 13m}}{{ - 13}} \\le \\frac{{65}}{{ - 13}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Switch the sign to ≤ since you divided by a negative number.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"m \\le  - 5\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>For the graph, shade to the left of <span data-math=\" - 5\"></span>to show all numbers left of <span data-math=\" - 5\"></span> are included, then put a bracket at <span data-math=\" - 5\"></span> to show that the solution includes <span data-math=\" - 5\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Write in interval notation with a parentheses and negative infinity on the left to show that the solution includes all numbers less than <span data-math=\" - 5\"></span>. After a comma, write <span data-math=\" - 5\"></span> with a bracket to show that <span data-math=\" - 5\"></span> is included in the solution.</p>\n<p>(–∞, –5]</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBamNKIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--764c713e2ad504ad673495891578e2f7bbaae9d7/CS_Figure_05_03_012.jpg\" alt=\"A number line ranges from negative 7 to negative 4, in increments of 1. A close square bracket is marked at negative 5. The region to the left of the square bracket is shaded on the number line. Text reads, m is less than or equal to negative 5, (negative infinity, negative 5)\">"
    }
   ],
